# ── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# No Python source is committed to this repository; it is declared as Markdown in
# jolarca-control/repos/jolarca-vendor.yml. These entries exist because Python is
# used as a build tool by `make yaml-check`, and because a local virtualenv is
# created by uv during development. See docs/ASSUMPTIONS.md decision D1.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/

# ── Node ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# markdownlint-cli2 is fetched on demand by npx and is never committed.
node_modules/
.markdownlint-cli2-*

# ── Editors and IDEs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ── Operating systems ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Secrets and local configuration ──────────────────────────────────────────
# This repository is PUBLIC. There is no legitimate reason for an environment
# file here, and no .env.example is provided either: a template invites someone to
# create the real file beside it. If configuration is ever needed, that is a
# signal the content belongs in a different repository.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.enc.yaml
*.enc.json
secrets/

# ── Confidential vendor content ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Belt-and-braces ignore rules for artifact classes that must never be committed
# here. They are `confidential` and belong in jolarca-compliance or jolarca-legal.
# Ignoring a path does not make committing it safe — see SECURITY.md — but it
# stops an accidental drag-and-drop from being staged.
#
# Every pattern is ANCHORED with a leading slash so it matches only at the
# repository root. An unanchored `evidence/` would also match docs/evidence/,
# which is legitimate published content, and git will not descend into an ignored
# directory to apply a later negation — the exclusion would win silently. Anchoring
# removes the need for a negation rule at all.
/vendor-assessments/
/vendor-evidence/
/transfer-impact-assessments/
/evidence/
/contracts/
*-assessment.md
*-dpa.md
*-scc.pdf
*-aoc.pdf
